1
00:00:07,851 --> 00:00:10,666
You must return to your universe.
I must have my captain back.

2
00:00:10,786 --> 00:00:14,118
I shall operate the transporter.
You have 2 minutes and 10 seconds.

3
00:00:14,238 --> 00:00:15,831
For that time I have something to say...

4
00:00:16,072 --> 00:00:19,152
How long before the Halkan prediction
of galactic revolt is realized?

5
00:00:19,364 --> 00:00:21,098
Approximately 240 years.

6
00:00:21,218 --> 00:00:22,363
The inevitable outcome?

7
00:00:22,483 --> 00:00:24,236
The Empire shall be
overthrown, of course.

8
00:00:24,356 --> 00:00:27,462
The illogic of waste, Mr. Spock.

9
00:00:28,756 --> 00:00:31,744
A waste of lives, potential,
resources, time.

10
00:00:31,864 --> 00:00:34,660
I submit to you that
your Empire is illogical...

11
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:36,329
Because it cannot endure.

12
00:00:37,421 --> 00:00:39,709
I submit...
That you...

13
00:00:40,018 --> 00:00:41,166
...are illogical...

14
00:00:41,437 --> 00:00:42,707
To be a willing part of it.

15
00:00:42,827 --> 00:00:44,831
You have 1 minute
and 23 seconds.

16
00:00:44,951 --> 00:00:48,267
If change is inevitable,
predictable, beneficial...

17
00:00:48,387 --> 00:00:51,370
Doesn't logic demand that
you be a part of it?

18
00:00:51,582 --> 00:00:53,200
One man cannot summon the future.

19
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:56,938
But one man can change the present.
Be the Captain of this Enterprise, Mr. Spock.

20
00:00:57,058 --> 00:01:00,314
Find a logical reason for sparing
the Halkans and make it stick.

21
00:01:00,434 --> 00:01:02,471
Push till it gives...

22
00:01:03,224 --> 00:01:05,199
You can defend yourself better
than any man in the fleet.

23
00:01:05,319 --> 00:01:07,307
Captain! Get in the chamber!

24
00:01:12,152 --> 00:01:13,774
What about it, Spock?

25
00:01:13,894 --> 00:01:16,293
A man must also have the power.

26
00:01:18,683 --> 00:01:20,036
In my cabin...

27
00:01:20,663 --> 00:01:23,952
...is a device that will
make you invincible.

28
00:01:24,072 --> 00:01:25,586
Indeed.

29
00:01:25,706 --> 00:01:28,879
What will it be?
Past or future? Tyranny or freedom?

30
00:01:28,999 --> 00:01:30,393
It's up to you.

31
00:01:42,526 --> 00:01:43,763
It is time.

32
00:01:44,198 --> 00:01:49,051
In every revolution there
is one man with a vision.

33
00:01:49,171 --> 00:01:54,304
[ENERGIZING]
Captain Kirk, I shall consider it.

34
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:13,082
[ENERGIZING]

35
00:02:19,691 --> 00:02:21,448
[ANGRY RANTS]

36
00:02:21,568 --> 00:02:24,460
KIRK:
What the devil is going
on, Mr. Spock?

37
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:27,973
It is agreeable to see
you again, Captain.

38
00:02:30,537 --> 00:02:33,528
It appears you were
temporarily interchanged...

39
00:02:33,648 --> 00:02:36,270
...with counterparts from
a parallel universe.

40
00:02:36,390 --> 00:02:39,011
Most of the crew is unaware
of these events.

41
00:02:39,925 --> 00:02:44,245
I know what happened, Spock.
I wanna know why. Who's responsible?

42
00:02:44,365 --> 00:02:48,150
The ion storm created a
transporter irregularity...

43
00:02:48,270 --> 00:02:52,152
Resulting in a transposition of the
landing party's quantum wave signatures.

44
00:02:52,272 --> 00:02:56,424
Chief Kyle was at the controls.
He has been disciplined.

45
00:02:56,544 --> 00:02:59,154
[CHUCKLES]
He'd better have been.

46
00:02:59,274 --> 00:03:00,734
- Mr. Scott.
- Sir?

47
00:03:00,854 --> 00:03:03,952
Check the transporter relays.
Make sure this doesn't happen again.

48
00:03:05,762 --> 00:03:08,635
I trust the Halkans have
been dealt with?

49
00:03:14,008 --> 00:03:16,622
Apparently I have to do
everything myself, don't I.

50
00:03:18,041 --> 00:03:20,684
Kirk to Bridge.
Is the Halkan capital city in firing range?

51
00:03:20,804 --> 00:03:22,380
Coming around again
in 4 minutes, sir.

52
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:23,931
Good.
On my way.

53
00:03:24,051 --> 00:03:26,172
MARLENA:
Welcome back, captain.

54
00:03:26,976 --> 00:03:28,557
See you in my quarters.

55
00:03:44,869 --> 00:03:46,248
Captain on the bridge.

56
00:03:49,121 --> 00:03:51,103
Lieutenant.
Get the Halkans on screen.

57
00:03:52,367 --> 00:03:53,919
Where's my navigator?

58
00:03:54,039 --> 00:03:55,346
Captain...?
Mr. Chekov...

59
00:03:55,375 --> 00:03:57,462
Ensign Chekov.
Return to your station immediately.

60
00:03:57,582 --> 00:04:02,137
It is merciful of you to forgive Mr. Chekov
after his assassination attempt.

61
00:04:03,564 --> 00:04:06,236
I agree that the agony booth made
a sufficient impression.

62
00:04:09,445 --> 00:04:11,331
What's the holdup, lieutenant?
Do you have them?

63
00:04:12,375 --> 00:04:14,683
Council-leader Tharn standing by.

64
00:04:17,479 --> 00:04:21,539
Your time has run out.
I'm tired of playing with you.

65
00:04:21,659 --> 00:04:24,432
This is no game, Captain Kirk.

66
00:04:24,451 --> 00:04:26,002
Oh, no.
It's not.

67
00:04:26,122 --> 00:04:29,564
You have 30 seconds to relinquish
your dilithium crystals.

68
00:04:29,593 --> 00:04:32,054
Or this face is the
last one you'll see.

69
00:04:32,174 --> 00:04:34,717
That would be most unwise, captain.

70
00:04:34,837 --> 00:04:39,237
But we are prepared to die to
protect what we hold dear.

71
00:04:40,156 --> 00:04:42,857
Have it your way.
Start the countdown. Ready phasers.

72
00:04:42,898 --> 00:04:43,779
Wait...

73
00:04:45,177 --> 00:04:47,437
Load photon torpedo tubes.

74
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:49,391
Full spread.

75
00:04:49,726 --> 00:04:51,057
SPOCK:
Captain...

76
00:04:51,086 --> 00:04:53,595
The Halkans have no
planetary defense grid.

77
00:04:53,715 --> 00:04:56,142
A torpedo barrage is unnecessary.

78
00:04:56,343 --> 00:05:00,068
The radiation fallout would likely
annihilate the entire population.

79
00:05:00,097 --> 00:05:01,122
Likely...

80
00:05:01,457 --> 00:05:05,508
Fitting isn't it? An example to
all who defy the Empire.

81
00:05:06,715 --> 00:05:08,553
Captain.
If I may...

82
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,333
Logic dictates that the survival
of the Halkan civilization...

83
00:05:14,453 --> 00:05:18,269
...could prove profitable for the
Empire for many years to come.

84
00:05:19,016 --> 00:05:22,895
You could be the first to set
the precedent of diplomacy...

85
00:05:23,015 --> 00:05:28,360
...that could yield long-term benefits.
I would recommend lesser measures.

86
00:05:31,312 --> 00:05:34,358
You've given me much to
think about, Mr. Spock.

87
00:05:37,806 --> 00:05:38,869
Fire.

88
00:05:55,038 --> 00:05:56,331
KIRK (VO):
Space...

89
00:05:56,451 --> 00:05:58,399
The final conquest.

90
00:06:05,927 --> 00:06:08,541
These are the voyages of
the Starship Enterprise.

91
00:06:09,863 --> 00:06:11,501
Its continuing mission...

92
00:06:11,621 --> 00:06:14,690
To discover and subjugate
strange new worlds.

93
00:06:14,810 --> 00:06:18,439
To advance our dominion and
vanquish all who stand against us.

94
00:06:18,812 --> 00:06:21,887
To conquer the galaxy for
the glory of the Empire.

95
00:07:03,050 --> 00:07:05,090
SPOCK (VO):
First officer's personal log.

96
00:07:05,210 --> 00:07:08,250
Captain Kirk has annihilated
the Halkan people...

97
00:07:08,370 --> 00:07:10,865
and I was unable to prevent it.

98
00:07:11,238 --> 00:07:13,221
I find myself torn...

99
00:07:14,226 --> 00:07:19,628
between loyalty to the Empire... and the
logic which predicts its inevitable demise.

100
00:07:20,633 --> 00:07:22,443
Status report.

101
00:07:22,563 --> 00:07:26,369
All torpedoes impacted, Captain.
The Halkan cities have been destroyed.

102
00:07:26,489 --> 00:07:28,064
Thank you, Jones.

103
00:07:28,184 --> 00:07:29,644
The name's Smith, sir.

104
00:07:29,764 --> 00:07:32,058
Mr. Spock, would you mind
telling me what just happened?

105
00:07:32,178 --> 00:07:34,787
Since when do you question
Imperial orders?

106
00:07:34,907 --> 00:07:38,809
I merely pointed out the obvious advantages
of an alternate course of action.

107
00:07:38,929 --> 00:07:41,079
Which you elected to ignore.

108
00:07:44,268 --> 00:07:47,429
Uhura. Contact Starfleet.
Let them know that we...

109
00:07:47,831 --> 00:07:50,043
That I have completed the mission.

110
00:07:50,163 --> 00:07:53,721
Notify them that strip-mining of the
planet's dilithium can proceed.

111
00:07:54,094 --> 00:07:55,186
Also...

112
00:07:55,579 --> 00:07:58,251
Make note of Mr. Spock's objection.

113
00:07:58,768 --> 00:08:00,061
Aye, sir.

114
00:08:01,526 --> 00:08:03,710
Ensign Chekov reporting for...

115
00:08:05,175 --> 00:08:07,962
Captain. I wish to thank you for
permitting me to resume my duties.

116
00:08:08,082 --> 00:08:11,639
- I trust you've learned your lesson, ensign?
- Yes sir!

117
00:08:13,363 --> 00:08:15,633
- Take him back to the agony booth.
- But, captain...

118
00:08:15,753 --> 00:08:17,903
- I changed my mind.
- But sir, you said...!

119
00:08:18,023 --> 00:08:20,316
I changed my mind!
[CHEKOV SCREAMS]

120
00:08:20,436 --> 00:08:23,189
Lieutenant. Have Mr. Leslie
report to the navigation station.

121
00:08:23,309 --> 00:08:25,315
UHURA: Aye, sir.
SMITH: Captain...

122
00:08:26,862 --> 00:08:29,563
I'm reading additional detonations
beneath the planet's crust.

123
00:08:29,683 --> 00:08:31,201
What sort of detonations?

124
00:08:31,321 --> 00:08:35,050
It looks like our torpedo barrage triggered
a reaction in the planet's dilithium strata.

125
00:08:35,170 --> 00:08:37,234
The crystal lattices are
being destroyed.

126
00:08:37,354 --> 00:08:40,423
Piezoelectric charges, Captain.
No doubt planted by the Halkans.

127
00:08:40,543 --> 00:08:42,750
Kirk to transporter room.

128
00:08:42,870 --> 00:08:46,313
Scotty. Beam as many dilithium crystals
as possible directly to the cargo bay.

129
00:08:46,744 --> 00:08:50,163
Captain. With all those explosions
there's no way to get a lock.

130
00:08:50,283 --> 00:08:52,347
Besides, the transporter circuits are...

131
00:08:52,467 --> 00:08:55,335
I don't need excuses, Mr. Scott!
I need solutions!

132
00:08:55,455 --> 00:08:57,547
Are you capable of
providing them?

133
00:08:57,667 --> 00:08:59,299
I'll get right on it, sir.

134
00:09:01,417 --> 00:09:04,893
The dilithium was rigged to explode.

135
00:09:05,013 --> 00:09:06,588
Why didn't you detect that?

136
00:09:06,708 --> 00:09:09,634
Captain. I advised against
this course of action.

137
00:09:09,754 --> 00:09:11,214
The logical decision was...

138
00:09:11,334 --> 00:09:13,398
You're not paid to lecture me
in logic, Mr. Spock!

139
00:09:13,518 --> 00:09:15,035
You're paid to do your job!

140
00:09:15,155 --> 00:09:17,621
I believe I am, sir.

141
00:09:23,396 --> 00:09:24,775
I'll be in my quarters.

142
00:09:29,042 --> 00:09:31,571
- Lieutenant.
- Uh-uh, Commander. Don't look at me.

143
00:09:31,691 --> 00:09:35,334
The captain's enemies aren't around
long. And I don't intend to be one of them.

144
00:09:35,454 --> 00:09:36,512
Commander...

145
00:09:36,531 --> 00:09:39,223
Three Andorian vessels dropping out of
warp just outside the system.

146
00:09:43,599 --> 00:09:46,424
Computer.
Analysis of approaching ships.

147
00:09:46,641 --> 00:09:47,991
COMPUTER (VO):
Working.

148
00:09:48,111 --> 00:09:50,022
Kumari-class battle cruisers.

149
00:09:50,347 --> 00:09:53,058
Armaments: 180-degree particle cannons.

150
00:09:53,178 --> 00:09:55,423
Hull composition: duranium alloy.

151
00:09:56,199 --> 00:09:57,482
Top of the line.

152
00:09:57,837 --> 00:10:00,327
We're receiving a transmission
from the Andorians...

153
00:10:00,538 --> 00:10:03,555
They say they witnessed the
destruction of the Halkans....

154
00:10:04,597 --> 00:10:08,169
And they no longer recognize the
authority of the Terran Empire.

155
00:10:10,180 --> 00:10:11,636
It has begun.

156
00:10:12,718 --> 00:10:15,758
- What has?
- Revolution, Lieutenant.

157
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:18,104
Revolution.

158
00:10:25,036 --> 00:10:26,290
What's wrong?

159
00:10:26,779 --> 00:10:28,493
I'll tell you what's wrong...

160
00:10:28,927 --> 00:10:33,102
What's wrong has pointed ears
and a knack for insubordination.

161
00:10:36,481 --> 00:10:38,655
Spock's been the best first
officer I could ever hope for.

162
00:10:38,775 --> 00:10:40,609
What's he playing at?
[INTERCOM WHISTLE]

163
00:10:40,647 --> 00:10:42,658
SPOCK (VO):
Bridge to Captain Kirk.

164
00:10:43,348 --> 00:10:44,775
Speak of the devil.

165
00:10:50,924 --> 00:10:51,920
Captain here.

166
00:10:52,265 --> 00:10:53,165
Captain.

167
00:10:53,180 --> 00:10:57,154
Long range sensors detect Andorian
rebels on an intercept course.

168
00:10:57,547 --> 00:11:00,401
If they make any aggressive moves,
destroy them. Kirk out.

169
00:11:00,521 --> 00:11:01,406
Captain.

170
00:11:01,526 --> 00:11:03,265
The Andorian government will not...

171
00:11:03,303 --> 00:11:06,809
Once again offering your opinion
when none is requested!

172
00:11:06,929 --> 00:11:08,102
Destroy them!

173
00:11:09,078 --> 00:11:10,467
I will not.

174
00:11:14,143 --> 00:11:15,417
All right, Spock.

175
00:11:16,279 --> 00:11:17,677
You're angling for something.

176
00:11:18,558 --> 00:11:19,756
What is it you want?

177
00:11:20,225 --> 00:11:22,609
What did that imposter offer you?

178
00:11:23,310 --> 00:11:25,340
What he offered me, captain...

179
00:11:25,733 --> 00:11:27,438
...is something you cannot give.

180
00:11:32,554 --> 00:11:33,808
I was right.

181
00:11:34,718 --> 00:11:37,409
The whole galaxy has gone crazy.

182
00:11:41,823 --> 00:11:44,025
What happened while I was gone?

183
00:11:47,377 --> 00:11:49,829
The imposter has obviously
been in my chair.

184
00:11:50,814 --> 00:11:52,347
Where else has he been?

185
00:11:54,252 --> 00:11:56,292
[COY LAUGHTER]

186
00:12:13,104 --> 00:12:17,471
SPOCK:
The actions taken against the
Halkans have been illogical.

187
00:12:17,931 --> 00:12:20,229
They shall likely serve as a catalyst...

188
00:12:20,349 --> 00:12:23,102
Which may jeopardize the
Empire's very survival.

189
00:12:25,134 --> 00:12:27,146
There is, however...

190
00:12:27,266 --> 00:12:29,272
...a path to the future.

191
00:12:29,392 --> 00:12:32,662
But that future may not involve
our present command.

192
00:12:32,782 --> 00:12:34,271
Spock...

193
00:12:35,679 --> 00:12:38,609
We had a good run, you and I.

194
00:12:45,447 --> 00:12:47,458
[FIZZLES OUT]

195
00:12:48,819 --> 00:12:50,169
No.

196
00:12:51,663 --> 00:12:53,009
- No!
- James...

197
00:12:53,129 --> 00:12:54,962
What's wrong with it?
Why isn't it working?

198
00:12:55,082 --> 00:12:57,093
- I don't know.
- Why isn't it working?

199
00:13:08,566 --> 00:13:10,597
Security detail to my quarters.

200
00:13:13,326 --> 00:13:14,657
Belay that order.

201
00:13:19,055 --> 00:13:20,176
Kirk to Farrell.

202
00:13:20,434 --> 00:13:22,110
Farrell here, sir.

203
00:13:22,656 --> 00:13:25,692
Send two of my personal guards to
my cabin. On the double.

204
00:13:25,812 --> 00:13:26,875
On the double, sir.

205
00:13:26,904 --> 00:13:30,332
And keep this channel secure.
Kirk out.

206
00:13:33,617 --> 00:13:35,025
What are you gonna do?

207
00:13:37,425 --> 00:13:40,021
Put an end to this insanity
once and for all.

208
00:13:40,346 --> 00:13:41,342
Why?

209
00:13:43,442 --> 00:13:45,176
Worried about me?

210
00:13:45,453 --> 00:13:47,541
I am the captain's woman.

211
00:13:49,351 --> 00:13:50,970
You are.
Aren't you?

212
00:13:52,023 --> 00:13:52,904
Always.

213
00:14:05,385 --> 00:14:06,745
[DOOR BUZZES]

214
00:14:06,865 --> 00:14:07,741
Come.

215
00:14:08,919 --> 00:14:10,077
Captain.

216
00:14:10,623 --> 00:14:12,175
Escort me to the bridge.

217
00:14:12,295 --> 00:14:14,345
We're taking Commander
Spock into custody.

218
00:14:15,274 --> 00:14:16,223
Sir?

219
00:14:16,912 --> 00:14:18,808
Do you have a hearing
problem, mister?

220
00:14:18,928 --> 00:14:19,737
No, sir.

221
00:14:20,735 --> 00:14:22,066
Wait for me.

222
00:14:22,555 --> 00:14:24,394
I'll be back in an hour.

223
00:14:37,388 --> 00:14:40,395
Commander. What the captain's
asking for... it's not possible!

224
00:14:40,432 --> 00:14:42,338
Mr. Scott. I must speak with you.

225
00:14:42,458 --> 00:14:43,851
Off the record.

226
00:14:44,234 --> 00:14:44,943
Sir?

227
00:14:46,073 --> 00:14:48,094
When you were in the
other reality...

228
00:14:48,214 --> 00:14:49,549
What did you see?

229
00:14:51,782 --> 00:14:53,085
I... erm...

230
00:14:54,454 --> 00:14:56,063
I saw weakness, Commander.

231
00:14:56,504 --> 00:14:59,051
Perhaps what you saw...
was peace.

232
00:14:59,682 --> 00:15:01,482
Is that possible, Mr. Scott?

233
00:15:01,602 --> 00:15:04,451
Commander, that kind of talk will
only lead to one place.

234
00:15:04,470 --> 00:15:05,380
The agony booth!

235
00:15:06,270 --> 00:15:07,908
You speak of weakness...

236
00:15:09,631 --> 00:15:12,620
But the true weakness lies
within the Terran Empire.

237
00:15:13,198 --> 00:15:15,947
It is held together by
tenuous bonds of fear.

238
00:15:16,718 --> 00:15:19,112
The destruction of the
Halkan civilization...

239
00:15:19,141 --> 00:15:22,110
...will serve as the final straw
for the outer colonies.

240
00:15:22,311 --> 00:15:24,715
Insurrection was
inescapable.

241
00:15:24,955 --> 00:15:26,804
But it has now
been accelerated.

242
00:15:27,972 --> 00:15:30,510
We cannot survive a
full-scale rebellion.

243
00:15:31,343 --> 00:15:34,111
But the peace that you
witnessed over there...

244
00:15:34,797 --> 00:15:37,488
...is not impossible in our
reality as well.

245
00:15:38,484 --> 00:15:41,386
Mr. Spock!
What you're saying... it's...

246
00:15:41,942 --> 00:15:43,033
Mutiny.

247
00:15:49,463 --> 00:15:51,129
KIRK (VO):
Captain's log, supplemental.

248
00:15:51,249 --> 00:15:53,428
Something happened during
my time away from the Enterprise.

249
00:15:53,548 --> 00:15:56,531
Commander Spock has become
emboldened to seek the captain's chair.

250
00:15:56,651 --> 00:15:59,203
But he's questioned my
orders for the final time.

251
00:15:59,777 --> 00:16:01,789
Mr. Spock, you're
under arrest...

252
00:16:04,087 --> 00:16:05,926
Where's my science officer?

253
00:16:06,046 --> 00:16:07,543
I don't know sir, I...

254
00:16:19,842 --> 00:16:22,715
Where's Mr. Spock?

255
00:16:23,893 --> 00:16:27,226
I believe he's in the
transporter room, captain.

256
00:16:29,553 --> 00:16:30,645
Good girl.

257
00:16:33,661 --> 00:16:35,644
Phasers at the ready.

258
00:16:44,379 --> 00:16:46,879
I would not wanna be
Mr. Spock right now.

259
00:16:48,948 --> 00:16:51,303
I'm not even sure I
wanna be on this ship.

260
00:17:03,665 --> 00:17:05,389
Where's Mr. Spock?

261
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,860
- Captain...
- Where's Mr. Spock?

262
00:17:08,291 --> 00:17:10,618
What did you witness, crewman?

263
00:17:18,864 --> 00:17:20,846
Let's try this again...

264
00:17:20,966 --> 00:17:23,173
Mr. Spock is a traitor.

265
00:17:23,293 --> 00:17:25,414
I wanna know where he is.

266
00:17:28,490 --> 00:17:31,679
[ELECTRICAL CHARGE]
[SCREAMS]

267
00:17:34,121 --> 00:17:35,270
Take him to sickbay.

268
00:17:35,759 --> 00:17:37,454
Let McCoy reason with him.

269
00:17:55,603 --> 00:17:57,958
All hands, this is the captain.

270
00:17:58,078 --> 00:18:01,090
First Officer Spock has mutinied
and fled the bridge.

271
00:18:01,808 --> 00:18:05,630
He is to be incapacitated
on sight and placed under arrest.

272
00:18:06,204 --> 00:18:10,313
The crewman who accomplishes this
will be promoted two steps in grade.

273
00:18:10,433 --> 00:18:11,347
Kirk out.

274
00:18:11,467 --> 00:18:12,726
[PHASER FIRE]

275
00:18:15,772 --> 00:18:18,501
I suggest you put down
your weapon, laddie.

276
00:18:24,148 --> 00:18:26,906
[SCREAMS IN AGONY]

277
00:18:29,320 --> 00:18:30,957
Doctor.

278
00:18:31,532 --> 00:18:33,974
Another dose.

279
00:18:34,094 --> 00:18:37,020
I've never used this
much before.

280
00:18:38,140 --> 00:18:40,123
I wonder what'll happen.

281
00:18:44,662 --> 00:18:47,305
[SCREAMS IN PAIN]
[HEARTBEAT INCREASES]

282
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:54,047
Captain.
He's of no value dead.

283
00:19:02,723 --> 00:19:05,223
This isn't your day, is it?

284
00:19:05,970 --> 00:19:08,728
Dr. McCoy is really
enjoying this.

285
00:19:09,130 --> 00:19:11,572
Unless you want
him to continue...

286
00:19:12,032 --> 00:19:14,244
Where's Mr. Spock?

287
00:19:16,159 --> 00:19:17,165
He...

288
00:19:17,825 --> 00:19:20,296
He was headed to auxiliary control.

289
00:19:22,537 --> 00:19:24,692
With Mr. Scott.

290
00:19:28,226 --> 00:19:30,898
- He's all yours, Doctor.
- Yes, sir.

291
00:19:31,530 --> 00:19:34,920
And give that traitorous elf a slap
from me when you catch him, Jim.

292
00:19:35,380 --> 00:19:36,759
Oh no... [SCREAMS]

293
00:19:38,741 --> 00:19:40,292
Kirk to Security Chief Sulu.

294
00:19:44,286 --> 00:19:45,895
Sulu here.

295
00:19:46,015 --> 00:19:47,906
Take a team to auxiliary control.

296
00:19:48,026 --> 00:19:51,124
Apprehend Mr. Spock and
Lieutenant Commander Scott.

297
00:19:51,244 --> 00:19:53,308
Lethal force is authorized.

298
00:19:53,428 --> 00:19:54,744
Lethal force, captain?

299
00:19:54,864 --> 00:19:57,387
There'll likely be casualties...
on both sides.

300
00:19:57,507 --> 00:20:00,778
Then take Chekov and put him
in front. Kirk out.

301
00:20:01,525 --> 00:20:02,818
I've gotta go.

302
00:20:02,938 --> 00:20:06,438
Ohhh. Don't be such a
party pooper, Hikaru.

303
00:20:06,558 --> 00:20:07,999
I'm serious.

304
00:20:08,119 --> 00:20:11,993
It's not often the captain gives anyone
a second chance. I intend to take it.

305
00:20:12,113 --> 00:20:16,130
Besides... with Scott and
Spock outta the way...

306
00:20:16,250 --> 00:20:19,089
Guess who's next in line
for first officer?

307
00:20:19,209 --> 00:20:24,031
Of course...
And you'll give me that commendation?

308
00:20:24,151 --> 00:20:26,703
I told you I would, didn't I?

309
00:20:26,823 --> 00:20:29,850
- Same time next week?
- Always.

310
00:20:29,970 --> 00:20:32,838
You know you're my favorite.

311
00:20:34,504 --> 00:20:36,458
[McKENNAH SIGHS]

312
00:20:46,102 --> 00:20:47,596
I've locked out bridge control.

313
00:20:47,625 --> 00:20:50,776
Transferred navigation, helm, and
long range communications to us.

314
00:20:50,896 --> 00:20:54,033
Seal off the armory.
Secure as many decks as possible.

315
00:20:54,072 --> 00:20:54,972
Aye, sir.

316
00:20:56,772 --> 00:20:58,439
Thank you,
Mr. Scott.

317
00:21:00,057 --> 00:21:02,509
Broadcast this recording on
all ship channels.

318
00:21:39,207 --> 00:21:40,710
Their phasers...

319
00:21:42,329 --> 00:21:44,043
They're only set to stun!

320
00:21:44,682 --> 00:21:47,076
Murder is the way of the Empire.

321
00:21:47,363 --> 00:21:48,895
The way of the captain.

322
00:21:49,202 --> 00:21:51,213
A way that must change.

323
00:21:51,510 --> 00:21:53,301
Join us, Mr. Chekov!

324
00:21:54,139 --> 00:21:55,949
Be a part of the future!

325
00:21:56,159 --> 00:21:57,481
Not of the past.

326
00:22:13,632 --> 00:22:15,049
[RED ALERT KLAXON]

327
00:22:17,156 --> 00:22:18,104
Status report.

328
00:22:18,140 --> 00:22:19,988
The Andorian vessels have
entered orbit, sir.

329
00:22:19,998 --> 00:22:20,821
They're charging weapons.

330
00:22:20,941 --> 00:22:22,976
Sound general quarters.
Ready main phaser banks.

331
00:22:23,096 --> 00:22:24,815
They're demanding we
surrender, captain.

332
00:22:25,763 --> 00:22:27,832
That was a warning shot
across our bow.

333
00:22:27,952 --> 00:22:30,504
- Shields are holding.
- Warning shot? Cowards.

334
00:22:30,624 --> 00:22:32,716
Lock onto their lead
ship and fire.

335
00:22:32,836 --> 00:22:34,235
- Captain?
- I said "Fire"!

336
00:22:34,254 --> 00:22:35,116
Aye, sir!

337
00:22:37,778 --> 00:22:39,464
Weapons are locked out!

338
00:22:39,830 --> 00:22:41,467
Locked out from where?

339
00:22:41,506 --> 00:22:42,731
[BOSUN WHISTLE]

340
00:22:42,851 --> 00:22:45,681
SPOCK (VO):
Attention crew of the
I.S.S. Enterprise.

341
00:22:45,801 --> 00:22:47,472
This is First Officer Spock.

342
00:22:47,510 --> 00:22:52,015
By now you are aware of the annihilation
of the peaceful Halkan people.

343
00:22:53,213 --> 00:22:54,984
KIRK:
Lieutenant!
Kill that broadcast!

344
00:22:55,104 --> 00:22:59,036
SPOCK (VO):
This action has served only to hasten
the fall of the Terran Empire.

345
00:22:59,294 --> 00:23:02,905
A civilization built upon a legacy
of violence and terror cannot survive.

346
00:23:02,943 --> 00:23:05,098
- Kill that broadcast!
- I can't, sir!

347
00:23:05,432 --> 00:23:08,496
SPOCK (VO):
The time has come to
embrace a new vision.

348
00:23:08,516 --> 00:23:10,067
A vision of equality.

349
00:23:10,187 --> 00:23:12,605
Of morality.
Of galactic peace.

350
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:15,995
A philosophy based upon
infinite diversity...

351
00:23:16,307 --> 00:23:17,964
...infinite combinations.

352
00:23:18,084 --> 00:23:20,492
This future is within our reach.

353
00:23:20,612 --> 00:23:22,772
But not under our
present command.

354
00:23:22,892 --> 00:23:24,103
Join me.

355
00:23:24,223 --> 00:23:28,024
Together we shall be the
architects of our own future.

356
00:23:33,383 --> 00:23:34,820
KIRK (VO):
Captain's log, supplemental.

357
00:23:34,940 --> 00:23:37,530
The Andorians are seeking
vengeance for the Halkans.

358
00:23:37,650 --> 00:23:40,806
And First Officer Spock is a
traitor to me and the Empire.

359
00:23:41,258 --> 00:23:43,509
I will not lose the Enterprise.

360
00:23:45,577 --> 00:23:47,493
Our shields won't hold
forever, commander.

361
00:23:52,657 --> 00:23:55,310
Sir, she said she needed
to speak with you.

362
00:23:56,478 --> 00:23:58,451
She poses no threat.

363
00:24:02,813 --> 00:24:05,619
Commander. We need to get
to Captain Kirk's quarters. Quickly!

364
00:24:05,739 --> 00:24:07,812
Lieutenant Moreau, it would
be extremely unwise to...

365
00:24:07,831 --> 00:24:09,105
Dammit, Mr. Spock!

366
00:24:09,225 --> 00:24:11,863
I can help.
Just come with me. Please!

367
00:24:15,403 --> 00:24:16,409
Mr. Scott.

368
00:24:16,964 --> 00:24:19,004
Encode a message
to the Andorians.

369
00:24:19,124 --> 00:24:21,791
Inform them that we have
control of the Enterprise...

370
00:24:22,604 --> 00:24:24,970
...and we are prepared to
join their cause.

371
00:24:25,525 --> 00:24:27,690
I shall return momentarily.

372
00:24:31,148 --> 00:24:32,843
Or you won't return at all.

373
00:24:34,375 --> 00:24:36,319
[SPOCK'S RECORDING REPEATS]

374
00:24:36,769 --> 00:24:39,633
Lieutenant!
Shut off that damn recording!

375
00:24:42,393 --> 00:24:44,969
Sir, the Andorians are powering
down their weapons.

376
00:24:44,988 --> 00:24:48,072
I'm detecting a transmission
from auxiliary control, captain.

377
00:24:48,637 --> 00:24:50,102
We're suing for peace.

378
00:24:50,428 --> 00:24:51,788
The hell we are...!

379
00:24:52,537 --> 00:24:54,127
Where's Mr. Leslie?

380
00:24:54,749 --> 00:24:56,722
Mr. Leslie didn't report
for duty, sir.

381
00:24:56,761 --> 00:24:59,212
Well get someone up
here to cover his shift!

382
00:24:59,332 --> 00:25:01,405
I want a navigator!
I want one now!

383
00:25:02,238 --> 00:25:03,778
So, this is it?!

384
00:25:03,779 --> 00:25:05,379
This is what I've got to work with?!

385
00:25:05,408 --> 00:25:07,169
I can navigate
the Enterprise, sir.

386
00:25:07,170 --> 00:25:08,530
Whatever you want.

387
00:25:10,139 --> 00:25:12,437
Set a course for Starbase 34.
Maximum warp.

388
00:25:15,727 --> 00:25:19,003
I'm sorry, captain! The controls
aren't responding! I tried! I can't!

389
00:25:19,443 --> 00:25:21,349
You say you can pilot my ship!

390
00:25:21,469 --> 00:25:23,379
You can't even get us out of orbit!

391
00:25:23,499 --> 00:25:25,529
Navigation has been rerouted
to auxiliary control.

392
00:25:25,557 --> 00:25:26,946
There's nothing I can do.

393
00:25:26,984 --> 00:25:29,149
Lieutenant.
You're relieved of your commission.

394
00:25:29,269 --> 00:25:30,557
Report to the brig.

395
00:25:30,677 --> 00:25:32,451
- Sir?
- Captain, it's not her fault!

396
00:25:32,489 --> 00:25:34,261
I said report to the brig!

397
00:25:34,280 --> 00:25:35,314
That's enough!

398
00:25:36,962 --> 00:25:39,337
We found him unconscious
on deck 8, sir.

399
00:25:39,567 --> 00:25:40,965
Chekov and the other men...

400
00:25:41,288 --> 00:25:42,850
They've turned.

401
00:25:49,458 --> 00:25:51,047
Resume your post.

402
00:25:56,145 --> 00:25:57,888
Am I not merciful?

403
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:01,125
Sulu.
You've got the conn.

404
00:26:03,367 --> 00:26:05,283
I want control of my ship!

405
00:26:05,637 --> 00:26:07,686
Or it's the booth for the lot of you!

406
00:26:18,815 --> 00:26:20,443
What are you looking at?

407
00:26:20,563 --> 00:26:22,876
You heard the captain.
Get to work.

408
00:26:31,914 --> 00:26:33,733
I was hoping you'd come
back during my shift.

409
00:26:33,853 --> 00:26:36,461
Oh.
You happy to see me?

410
00:26:36,758 --> 00:26:37,898
Always.

411
00:26:53,667 --> 00:26:57,058
The device of which the other
captain spoke, I presume.

412
00:26:57,479 --> 00:27:00,764
I am surprised Captain Kirk
did not use it on me.

413
00:27:01,224 --> 00:27:03,493
Oh.
He tried.

414
00:27:16,174 --> 00:27:17,534
Fascinating.

415
00:27:18,540 --> 00:27:20,857
James met an alien scientist...

416
00:27:20,876 --> 00:27:23,520
...at the Starfleet penal colony
on Tantalus Five.

417
00:27:23,746 --> 00:27:27,117
He pillaged her laboratory
after he dispensed with her.

418
00:27:27,453 --> 00:27:29,560
Then he stole this device.

419
00:27:30,508 --> 00:27:33,975
One touch and your problems
are over, Mr. Spock.

420
00:27:36,300 --> 00:27:37,976
This'll change everything.

421
00:27:39,930 --> 00:27:42,707
You would see me use
this device on him?

422
00:27:46,014 --> 00:27:46,982
I would.

423
00:27:47,796 --> 00:27:49,213
But you...

424
00:27:50,075 --> 00:27:52,124
...are the captain's woman.

425
00:27:53,398 --> 00:27:54,250
Yes.

426
00:27:56,154 --> 00:27:58,155
But not this captain.

427
00:28:20,137 --> 00:28:24,734
No revolution can succeed using the same
methods which failed in the previous one.

428
00:28:26,573 --> 00:28:27,856
Commander...

429
00:28:28,383 --> 00:28:30,068
Spock...

430
00:28:32,038 --> 00:28:33,982
Please find a way.

431
00:28:34,968 --> 00:28:37,382
A way to send me where he went.

432
00:28:38,741 --> 00:28:40,293
I cannot.

433
00:28:40,494 --> 00:28:41,538
Please!

434
00:28:42,343 --> 00:28:44,287
It is not within my power.

435
00:28:46,194 --> 00:28:48,368
But you can make
a difference here.

436
00:29:23,404 --> 00:29:25,846
All clear, sir.

437
00:29:25,966 --> 00:29:27,972
Wait outside.

438
00:29:56,327 --> 00:29:59,602
Captain Kirk to Mr. Spock.

439
00:30:00,177 --> 00:30:02,504
Captain Kirk to Mr. Spock.

440
00:30:03,225 --> 00:30:05,581
Mr. Spock. Come in please.

441
00:30:09,575 --> 00:30:11,155
Spock here.

442
00:30:11,275 --> 00:30:12,649
Commander.

443
00:30:12,769 --> 00:30:16,815
There's no reason we can't talk
about this like civilized men.

444
00:30:17,878 --> 00:30:21,986
I've listened to your logic
and I find it compelling.

445
00:30:22,532 --> 00:30:25,233
There's merit in what
you say, Spock.

446
00:30:25,808 --> 00:30:28,796
I see the potential for change.

447
00:30:29,428 --> 00:30:32,703
The opportunity to better
the Empire.

448
00:30:35,898 --> 00:30:37,420
Spock...

449
00:30:38,167 --> 00:30:39,977
I have the bridge.

450
00:30:40,097 --> 00:30:42,420
You have auxiliary control.

451
00:30:42,540 --> 00:30:44,890
Who makes the next move?

452
00:30:45,350 --> 00:30:47,246
What do you propose?

453
00:30:47,907 --> 00:30:49,258
We meet...

454
00:30:49,378 --> 00:30:50,637
Somewhere neutral...

455
00:30:50,662 --> 00:30:51,887
Half an hour.

456
00:30:52,970 --> 00:30:55,105
Deck 5.
Officer's lounge.

457
00:30:55,474 --> 00:30:57,466
No weapons.
No tricks.

458
00:30:57,906 --> 00:30:59,419
Just you and I.

459
00:31:02,915 --> 00:31:05,625
We've had many successes together, Spock.

460
00:31:07,369 --> 00:31:09,993
I know we can work this out.

461
00:31:15,946 --> 00:31:18,129
Very well.
Half an hour.

462
00:31:18,771 --> 00:31:20,619
You don't actually
trust him, do you?

463
00:31:20,739 --> 00:31:21,797
Of course not.

464
00:31:21,836 --> 00:31:24,239
It's some kind of set-up!
Why play his game?

465
00:31:25,230 --> 00:31:27,979
If there is any hope for
the Empire to change...

466
00:31:28,007 --> 00:31:31,158
I must give Captain Kirk the
opportunity to do so as well.

467
00:31:55,090 --> 00:31:57,417
Captain...

468
00:31:57,952 --> 00:31:59,992
Commander...

469
00:32:01,313 --> 00:32:02,922
No weapons.

470
00:32:10,920 --> 00:32:14,166
I've considered our game
while you were away.

471
00:32:14,540 --> 00:32:17,068
Bishop to queen's level two.

472
00:32:17,585 --> 00:32:19,769
Knight takes bishop.

473
00:32:20,229 --> 00:32:22,642
You've left your king vulnerable.

474
00:32:23,016 --> 00:32:25,228
As have you.

475
00:32:26,262 --> 00:32:28,895
Seems we're at a stalemate.

476
00:32:32,141 --> 00:32:34,268
Spock...

477
00:32:34,388 --> 00:32:36,164
You can't win.

478
00:32:36,767 --> 00:32:40,100
What's your next move?
Kill me? Take command of the Enterprise?

479
00:32:40,220 --> 00:32:43,634
There are a dozen starships out
there. All loyal to the Empire.

480
00:32:43,754 --> 00:32:45,329
As am I.

481
00:32:45,449 --> 00:32:49,093
But the Empire as it stands
today is at a crossroads.

482
00:32:49,213 --> 00:32:52,023
Eventually all kings are vulnerable.

483
00:32:57,354 --> 00:33:00,773
He put these thoughts into that Vulcan
head of yours, didn't he? That...

484
00:33:00,893 --> 00:33:02,985
That other captain.

485
00:33:04,738 --> 00:33:05,945
Spock...

486
00:33:06,835 --> 00:33:09,450
After all we've been through.
All we've accomplished.

487
00:33:09,488 --> 00:33:11,720
Earned for ourselves!

488
00:33:12,150 --> 00:33:15,378
You would trust a stranger
from another universe?

489
00:33:16,115 --> 00:33:17,667
I believe I would.

490
00:33:18,030 --> 00:33:21,593
That captain had a vision of an
imminent future which you fail to see.

491
00:33:23,671 --> 00:33:27,090
Then you're an even bigger
fool than I imagined.

492
00:33:33,311 --> 00:33:35,040
Your mutiny ends.

493
00:33:35,160 --> 00:33:37,248
Right here and now.

494
00:33:49,503 --> 00:33:52,862
You didn't really think I'd let you
walk out of here did you?

495
00:33:53,297 --> 00:33:57,583
And now it comes to this.
Checkmate.

496
00:33:58,886 --> 00:34:00,421
Perhaps not.

497
00:34:00,541 --> 00:34:05,084
Mr. Scott implemented a level 3
energy dampening field on this deck.

498
00:34:05,519 --> 00:34:08,589
Yet another act of treachery...
which proves, once again...

499
00:34:08,709 --> 00:34:11,456
...why your command must
come to an end.

500
00:34:13,643 --> 00:34:14,570
Report!

501
00:34:14,690 --> 00:34:17,843
The tectonic explosions are
destabilizing the planet's orbit!

502
00:34:26,242 --> 00:34:29,109
We've run simulations of dilithium
generator strata in the chem lab.

503
00:34:29,229 --> 00:34:30,992
I've seen this sort
of thing before!

504
00:34:31,484 --> 00:34:34,786
The Andorian ships have broken
orbit and gone to warp, sir!

505
00:34:34,906 --> 00:34:36,379
They've got the right idea, lad!

506
00:34:36,499 --> 00:34:38,377
Put some distance between
us and that planet!

507
00:34:52,454 --> 00:34:53,931
There's that human side!

508
00:34:54,051 --> 00:34:57,059
I always knew you'd kill me
to get the captain's chair!

509
00:34:57,179 --> 00:34:59,607
You're no better than
the rest of us...!

510
00:35:05,921 --> 00:35:08,267
[KIRK GASPS FOR AIR]

511
00:35:19,310 --> 00:35:21,540
Captain Kirk.

512
00:35:21,660 --> 00:35:23,712
The future is coming.

513
00:35:23,832 --> 00:35:25,421
You are the past.

514
00:35:25,541 --> 00:35:27,477
I offer this crew an alternative.

515
00:35:27,597 --> 00:35:28,636
This crew...

516
00:35:28,756 --> 00:35:30,489
This crew?

517
00:35:30,609 --> 00:35:32,545
They don't need alternatives.
They're pawns.

518
00:35:32,665 --> 00:35:34,023
Pawns need a king!

519
00:35:34,143 --> 00:35:36,600
They serve for my conquests.
My victories!

520
00:35:36,720 --> 00:35:39,062
You think they're smart
enough to follow you?

521
00:35:39,182 --> 00:35:40,955
They're mine!
I can use them!

522
00:35:40,964 --> 00:35:42,953
Break them!
Send them to their own slaughter!

523
00:35:43,007 --> 00:35:44,578
And they'll thank me for it!

524
00:35:48,562 --> 00:35:55,281
[KIRK'S SPEECH ECHOES SHIPWIDE]

525
00:36:10,935 --> 00:36:14,092
You double-crossing
half-breed traitor!

526
00:36:14,212 --> 00:36:18,321
James T. Kirk.
You are hereby relieved of command.

527
00:36:19,161 --> 00:36:20,319
Let go of me!

528
00:36:20,439 --> 00:36:22,202
Do you realize
what you're doing?!

529
00:36:27,708 --> 00:36:28,663
I do.

530
00:36:42,189 --> 00:36:44,158
KIRK:
You're a coward, Spock.

531
00:36:44,593 --> 00:36:47,779
You don't even have the guts
to execute us like a real leader.

532
00:36:47,899 --> 00:36:50,385
This shuttlecraft is at
your disposal.

533
00:36:50,820 --> 00:36:53,918
I recommend setting a course
to the nearest habitable system.

534
00:36:54,295 --> 00:36:56,612
You have sufficient supplies
to last until then.

535
00:36:56,732 --> 00:36:58,772
You think that changes anything?

536
00:36:58,892 --> 00:37:02,914
So you've taken control of one ship.
So what? What now?

537
00:37:03,522 --> 00:37:05,144
Peace?

538
00:37:05,636 --> 00:37:07,056
Freedom?

539
00:37:07,837 --> 00:37:11,371
The Empire will hunt you down
like the mangy dog that you are.

540
00:37:13,022 --> 00:37:14,122
Perhaps...

541
00:37:14,499 --> 00:37:15,918
But I must try...

542
00:37:28,904 --> 00:37:31,018
You won't get away
with this, Spock.

543
00:37:31,138 --> 00:37:33,509
You're just one man.

544
00:37:33,629 --> 00:37:37,042
In every revolution there is
one man with a vision.

545
00:37:37,708 --> 00:37:39,446
Who told you that?

546
00:37:40,547 --> 00:37:41,792
You did.

547
00:37:42,921 --> 00:37:45,586
Spock...!!!

548
00:37:45,706 --> 00:37:48,453
[KIRK'S CRY CONTINUES TO ECHO]

549
00:38:15,885 --> 00:38:18,607
Commander.
Status report.

550
00:38:19,850 --> 00:38:23,818
All decks reporting in, captain.
The Halkan survivors are safely on board.

551
00:38:23,938 --> 00:38:27,236
Shuttlecraft Galileo is
leaving sensor range.

552
00:38:33,318 --> 00:38:36,330
James T. Kirk chose his path.

553
00:38:36,706 --> 00:38:39,371
It is time we chose ours.

554
00:38:39,491 --> 00:38:40,964
Warp two, ensign.

555
00:38:41,084 --> 00:38:42,889
Heading, sir?

556
00:38:46,770 --> 00:38:48,942
Forward.

557
00:40:19,807 --> 00:40:25,748
English subtitles by:
Peter Goundrill

